// 0b prefixed integers, then an imaginary literal (its `j` suffix follows the same
// magnitude as a real one), then reals. `_` separators are allowed between digits -
// and, as CPython also accepts, right after the base prefix - and are stripped
// before the value is read. A real is an integer, or a float with a fraction
// (leading digits optional: `.5`; trailing digits optional: `5.`), or an exponent
// form. Whitespace skipping is off from the second character on, so `0 x1`, `1 . 5`
// and `1 j` are not literals. An integer too large for a double becomes a boxed
