            // residue of 51436f9 (which did the list surface). A set is a dict
            // whose keys ARE its members here, so both live in this branch and
            // the SET is asked first. The twins are pySetMethod/pyDictMethod in
            // abnf/jsrt.go and in languages/lib/python-rt.metajs.
            //
            // A name the OTHER type owns raises AttributeError, which is what
            // CPython does - and the two "only" lists are narrower than the two
            // method sets, because pop/clear/copy/update are on BOTH types.
            // Asking one type for the other's name used to answer: `set().keys()`
            // was the member list in this half and aborted with "unknown method
